{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>Which I have reserved for a time of distress</b> — like: 'He cast down great stones and hail,' which was in Egypt. And the Gaon [Saadia] interpreted: what is the way that light dwells upon a place that exists on earth, where it is darkness entirely except for one day. And the opposite case, a place where the light is [present] half a year — even though his words are correct, they are not from the subject of the verses. And so he interpreted 'what is the way that light is distributed.' Some say: that this light is rain."], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 38, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:05:04.383551113Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}